 "poem": "Glared gleam from the lurid light\nOf wedlock and marriage and\nDisease of hate, the disease\nOf which the hands are moist with fire.\nThe eyes in grey were full again\nWith blood that had been dry before them.\nThey fought for two and seven hundred\nAnd fifty years, over many,\nThrough many a burning day,\nBlazing all night through to morning,\nTill one at last was given voice again,\nAnd blithe-birded breath in sleepless heaven",
